#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166456 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c20cd9a-5734-5129-93db-55f6dc985b3a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing the Formulas for Variation of Parameters"}] :question/id #uuid "6060e2fe-05b3-587d-b5dd-3cdab705eb05" :question/math-academy-id "e-21546" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t) =\nA\n\\mathbf{x}(t) +\n\\mathbf{f}(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)  = \\Phi \\mathbf{u}(t),$ where $\\Phi$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $\\mathbf{u}(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for $\\mathbf x_p(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\textrm{L1}{:}\\:$ $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)  = \\Phi \\mathbf{u}(t)$\n\n$\\textrm{L2}{:}\\:$ $\\mathbf{x}'_p(t) = \\Phi \\mathbf{u}'(t) + \\Phi' \\mathbf{u}(t)$\n\n$\\textrm{L3}{:}\\:$ $\\Phi \\mathbf{u}'(t) + \\Phi' \\mathbf{u}(t) = A \\Phi \\mathbf{u}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t)$\n\n$\\textrm{L4}{:}\\:$ $\\Phi' = A \\Phi$\n\n$\\textrm{L5}{:}\\:$ $\\Phi \\mathbf{u}'(t) = \\mathbf{f}(t)$\n\n$\\textrm{L6}{:}\\:$ $\\mathbf{u}'(t) = \\Phi^{-1}(t) \\mathbf{f}(t)$\n\n$\\textrm{L7}{:}\\:$ $\\displaystyle\\mathbf{u}(t) = \\int \\Phi^{-1} \\mathbf{f}(t) \\, \\text{d}t$\n\n$\\textrm{L8}{:}\\:$ $\\displaystyle\\mathbf{x}_p(t) = \\Phi \\int \\Phi^{-1}\\mathbf{f}(t) \\, \\text{d}t$\n\nFill in the blanks with the correct reasons to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L4}$ follows from the fact that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071383/assets/81e146c6f6297f8f30340d63ddaec02efe3d6442005f5852a70d5be22ceed764.png) matrix.\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L6}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L5}$ by  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071383/assets/09febb48bb00d22caebf088103181b5db6377befccad18f1370718351cc91e9d.png) both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\textrm{L7}$ into ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071383/assets/9be3bba9e4f49ae67d635fe7b6260607d3e776f03baeaf8d5a10d650e0b0b987.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider line $\\textrm{L4}.$ Since $\\Phi$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions to the homogeneous system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) =A\\mathbf{x}(t),$ i.e., by substituting any column $\\mathbf{c}(t)$ of $\\Phi$ into the homogeneous system, we get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c}'(t) =A\\mathbf{c}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{c}'(t)$ is the corresponding column of derivatives in $\\Phi.$ As a result, this means that $\\Phi' = A \\Phi.$ Therefore, $\\textrm{L4}$ follows from the fact that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071383/assets/f3cf7b9339acd3d9b370c67a182509bff354728494afda00e2e991f3a09996af.png) matrix.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\textrm{L5}$ and $\\textrm{L6}.$ Since $\\Phi$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are linearly independent. So, $\\Phi$ is invertible. Therefore, $\\textrm{L6}$ follows from $\\textrm{L5}$ by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071383/assets/8ba4d14f89d4c90c90f84e0618b0cf8dedadbf2c3989cc9533e44590100357d1.png) both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\cdot Φ{u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ ({Φ}^{-1}Φ)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\textrm{L1},$ $\\textrm{L7},$ and $\\textrm{L8}.$ Substituting\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}(t) = \\int \\Phi^{-1} \\mathbf{f}(t) \\, \\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom $\\textrm{L7}$ into $\\textrm{L1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φu(t) \\\\  & =Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\textrm{L7}$ into  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071383/assets/4d1fa76e9619981c1b36c457c5247dad023bdbb7f7810fdc9e5b9105028c4e22.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166457 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d23f2a1-55fa-5398-9016-dc6fbc55c97b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Particular Solution of an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/id #uuid "1d203940-c05d-5f30-a8ad-c618d6d6ba5b" :question/math-academy-id "e-21547" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071383/assets/2b22742201ba6932de40a628419faef0405bc8ae0ad26814bc7ca515455e3e5c.png)\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute $\\Phi^{-1} \\, \\mathbf{f}(t)$ and the particular solution $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ of the system." :question/worked-solution "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}_p(t)  = \\Phi \\, \\mathbf{u}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $\\mathbf{f}(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}(t) = \\int \\Phi^{-1} \\, \\mathbf{f}(t) \\, \\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071383/assets/0c7accec33fc7c9d6b2a228c8ec4bcc454f687be7f96ab615b3b818f82fb8cc8.png)\n\nSince $\\Phi$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0\\cdot (-2{e}^{-4t})-2{e}^{-4t}\\cdot {e}^{3t}}[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{-4t} & -2{e}^{-4t} \\\\ -{e}^{3t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{-4t} & -2{e}^{-4t} \\\\ -{e}^{3t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{-3t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{-3t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4t} & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{-2t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $\\mathbf{u}(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{-2t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-2t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{10}{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2{e}^{-4t} \\\\ {e}^{3t} & -2{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-2t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{10}{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{t} \\\\ -\\frac{17}{10}{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{17}{10}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166458 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74dbd777-f24e-5d23-b495-a56710d71f5a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/id #uuid "ce663953-3e5e-55e2-a8db-6d7a531496cf" :question/math-academy-id "e-21548" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071383/assets/bc92d310e939c8688ab770a51107d1218d5b8878a877d7b3a64af770d002a9ca.png)\nConsider the system of differential equations. Using the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n| ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071383/assets/860251c7cc4c1259c4660b41aae1f3e0b0177e13c9372dd941422040f0f7e5ee.png) |  | $\\boxed{\\rule{0pt}{1.3em}\\phantom{xxxxxxxx}}$ |  | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\mathbf{x}_c(t) + \\mathbf{x}_p(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{x}_c(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nNotice that we are given that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071383/assets/e8db6a28a4671312259595de0609cefb8db0d5fc441e122885335e1165e0cd22.png)\n\nWe'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}_p(t)  = \\Phi \\, \\mathbf{u}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $\\mathbf{f}(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}(t) = \\int \\Phi^{-1} \\, \\mathbf{f}(t) \\, \\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071383/assets/742a0ea79220f0dc0055918b611393d69518bc5c73ef9b41b6fd068c8c75ad4c.png)\n\nSince $\\Phi$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{-2t}\\cdot {e}^{-4t}-0}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-4t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-4t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]. \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $\\mathbf{u}(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int 2t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int 0\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating the components by parts, we get the following:\n\n- For the first component, let $u=2t$ and $\\text{d}v=e^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=2\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=\\dfrac{1}{2}e^{2t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(2t)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}(2\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =t{e}^{2t}-\\int {e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =t{e}^{2t}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}(2t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, the integrand is zero, so the integral is zero.\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}(2t-1) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2t-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167113 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74dbd777-f24e-5d23-b495-a56710d71f5a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d427c70-395b-59f9-8a4e-a0096c7d539a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18t-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d427c70-395b-59f9-8a4e-a0096c7d539a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18t-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370883} :answer-field/id #uuid "60f42601-7e93-5cf0-afea-bec9263afe07" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6dc5997-1d4e-5312-9245-798d648973c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-329817" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}12t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations. Using the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n| $x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-12t-6$ |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nNotice that we are given that\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWe'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}12t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{-2t}\\cdot {e}^{t}-2{e}^{t}\\cdot 2{e}^{-2t}}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & -2{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{t}}{3}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & -2{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & -2{e}^{2t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-t} & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & -2{e}^{2t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-t} & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}12t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 8t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}-4t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 8t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int -4t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int 8t{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating the components by parts, we get the following:\n\n- For the first component, let $u=-4t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=-4\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -4t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(-4t)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}\\cdot (-4\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-2t{e}^{2t}+\\int 2{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2t{e}^{2t}+{e}^{2t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}(1-2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, let $u=8t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=8\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=-{e}^{-t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -4t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =8t\\cdot (-{e}^{-t})-\\int -{e}^{-t}\\cdot 8\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-8t{e}^{-t}+\\int 8\\,{e}^{-t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-8t{e}^{-t}-8{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =-8{e}^{-t}(1+t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}(1-2t) \\\\ -8{e}^{-t}(1+t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(1-2t)-16(1+t) \\\\ 2(1-2t)-8(1+t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-18t-15 \\\\ -12t-6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167122 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c20cd9a-5734-5129-93db-55f6dc985b3a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing the Formulas for Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8608eb86-7846-5c0c-a0b9-5483f7d412bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164089} {:answer/id #uuid "e19ba397-1218-5049-897b-7ec948b40ac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164090} {:answer/id #uuid "04bc74d5-6488-5f9c-89d3-179621597f13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164091} {:answer/id #uuid "3a55a84a-9e03-57e1-aafb-531f05c56719" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by $Φ^{− 1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04bc74d5-6488-5f9c-89d3-179621597f13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164091} :answer-field/id #uuid "d077fc5a-f837-562e-9934-ad718bd47619" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164088} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98df3017-3eb8-5507-8f5e-cc4b7f2bd8a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a fundamental" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164094} {:answer/id #uuid "00c41c96-848b-505c-873a-644562ac687f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is the identity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164095} {:answer/id #uuid "191f0574-5f11-578e-b6e8-ea18171c118d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is an invertible" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164096} {:answer/id #uuid "5b15dec5-2127-5197-9d03-d4353079b93c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a square" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98df3017-3eb8-5507-8f5e-cc4b7f2bd8a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a fundamental" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164094} :answer-field/id #uuid "2080a27e-dd12-5e6a-b899-ff1fd5f8be7f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164093} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2041cd9-ed52-5f7d-84eb-36b642efe80e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164099} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f76d10-414d-5b54-82d2-c7d0803a3f5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164100} {:answer/id #uuid "0accd6ae-e802-5ddb-82ef-e55bdbe02f90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164101} {:answer/id #uuid "5976edc2-fa65-5378-8a1b-b7af3df0e7bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by $Φ^{− 1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5976edc2-fa65-5378-8a1b-b7af3df0e7bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by $Φ^{− 1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164102} :answer-field/id #uuid "8261617f-ecee-5fd9-a564-c41fdc6ecae6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164098}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9ad3fcdc-246d-580f-b053-3062ecfa179a" :question/math-academy-id "q-330877" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that {{field-1}} matrix.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-2}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ i.e., by substituting any column $c(t)$ of $Φ$ into the homogeneous system, we get\n\n$$\n{c}^{′}(t)=Ac(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}^{′}(t)$ is the corresponding column of derivatives in $Φ.$ As a result, this means that ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that $Φ\\text{ is a fundamental}$ matrix.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are linearly independent. So, $Φ$ is invertible. Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{multiplying by }{Φ}^{-1}$ both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\cdot Φ{u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ ({Φ}^{-1}Φ)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167124 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d23f2a1-55fa-5398-9016-dc6fbc55c97b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Particular Solution of an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eea0e7a5-117d-520d-a8e3-af3023eede9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6e^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370884} {:answer/id #uuid "2d06b239-eb55-5256-8c69-6a5f81c7a750" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12e^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d06b239-eb55-5256-8c69-6a5f81c7a750" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12e^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370885} :answer-field/id #uuid "aba5c766-9160-5ecd-9315-0d4eaf8a41c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20b59e05-4f90-5449-9efd-04698ea2adf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370886}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20b59e05-4f90-5449-9efd-04698ea2adf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370886} :answer-field/id #uuid "206b1b63-7514-5b46-ba97-fea8ea4231de" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dc4c9e61-81e1-5e97-95cb-a89bd2a71a0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-330899" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -3\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}5{e}^{t} \\\\ 6{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]}},\\,Φ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t} & -6{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n| ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,,\\,$ | ${x}_{p}(t)={e}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | ${e}^{-t}$ |  |  | $9$ |  |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t} & -6{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5{e}^{t} \\\\ 6{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0\\cdot (-6{e}^{2t})-5{e}^{2t}\\cdot {e}^{-3t}}[\\begin{aligned}-6{e}^{2t} & -5{e}^{2t} \\\\ -{e}^{-3t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{t}}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-6{e}^{2t} & -5{e}^{2t} \\\\ -{e}^{-3t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-6{e}^{3t} & -5{e}^{3t} \\\\ -{e}^{-2t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-6{e}^{3t} & -5{e}^{3t} \\\\ -{e}^{-2t} & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5{e}^{t} \\\\ 6{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12{e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}12{e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int 12{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int {e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{4t} \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t} & -6{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{4t} \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5{e}^{t} \\\\ 9{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370887 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d23f2a1-55fa-5398-9016-dc6fbc55c97b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Particular Solution of an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38b6294c-18c9-5bd6-b5fe-6c318a036071" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3e^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370889} {:answer/id #uuid "db617487-9c49-56d9-a93b-47fc7444f682" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38b6294c-18c9-5bd6-b5fe-6c318a036071" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3e^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370889} :answer-field/id #uuid "17d79a92-2748-55e0-a38e-35a1b989a036" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370888} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4dfcfa5-1d69-5378-b3ff-281b6dd6eb78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4dfcfa5-1d69-5378-b3ff-281b6dd6eb78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370892} :answer-field/id #uuid "4973c3ce-d70b-5651-8464-19f378e73dc7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5410bedb-33cd-5e6c-885a-74e25e6e1037" :question/math-academy-id "q-336699" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}},\\,Φ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n| ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | $5{e}^{-t}$ |  | $\\,,\\,$ | ${x}_{p}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | $-4$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{3t}-({e}^{3t})\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & -{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & -{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5{e}^{-t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}5{e}^{-t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int 5{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int -3{e}^{-3t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167200 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c20cd9a-5734-5129-93db-55f6dc985b3a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing the Formulas for Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a40fb41-904d-581f-9085-4a80f508ca4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by $Φ^{− 1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164710} {:answer/id #uuid "54cc4d7e-999e-535e-8b7f-829d5f8a361b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164711} {:answer/id #uuid "620f0ef2-de67-5ea0-be3f-b1a901e676fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164712} {:answer/id #uuid "752ec359-a9d2-569a-b4ba-305559870367" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a40fb41-904d-581f-9085-4a80f508ca4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by $Φ^{− 1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164710} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e207189-d64b-57c9-893d-c96318522060" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164709} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98517f60-dd1c-5e01-ac7f-a08c5c8558c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is an invertible" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164715} {:answer/id #uuid "f5307e2a-39c8-5b17-b307-b9e8d5590c6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a fundamental" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164716} {:answer/id #uuid "0a8ddf49-18f6-5121-bbd9-fa8e15f3c65d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a square" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164717} {:answer/id #uuid "69f0b669-e69d-5b75-9e55-a76a16dd41a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is the identity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5307e2a-39c8-5b17-b307-b9e8d5590c6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a fundamental" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164716} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5c81b57-321a-5219-99a2-c7fccb4eb606" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164714} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "190f80f0-e123-5399-934c-1177d892e721" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164725} {:answer/id #uuid "1a4c5e67-5d3f-5c7c-945b-73bfd5ada9af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164726} {:answer/id #uuid "61c40f64-a096-5b92-b47d-bd4620a11ecd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164727} {:answer/id #uuid "7debf8c9-b398-50ee-aa43-2e1201ef8982" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by $Φ^{− 1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a4c5e67-5d3f-5c7c-945b-73bfd5ada9af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164726} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ae1cb92-929c-5a34-a92c-301d276151cb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164724} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "565eb9ba-a54a-5524-a2ad-b5d0b99d7f77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "line $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370894} {:answer/id #uuid "7fb02c88-36db-5d97-8f6d-fadde5f9b915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370895} {:answer/id #uuid "31a14f31-5666-593f-a097-a499d23c3d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "solution of the system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370896} {:answer/id #uuid "4e916a55-2d55-5da0-9277-78517961b9e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first shifting theorem" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fb02c88-36db-5d97-8f6d-fadde5f9b915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370895} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e11665d-81ce-5fef-a287-3cbfffa09549" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f3e98464-6e85-513e-a930-d0947c1c72b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-336711" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-1}} both sides of  the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that {{field-4}} matrix." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ To get $\\text{L2},$ we are $\\text{differentiating}$ with respect to $t$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =(Φu(t))^{′} \\\\ {x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L2},$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Let's substitute ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$ from $\\text{L1}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ into the initial system of ODEs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =Ax(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t) & =AΦu(t)+f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into $\\text{initial system of ODEs}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are linearly independent. So, $Φ$ is invertible. Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{pre-multiplying by }{Φ}^{-1}$ both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\cdot Φ{u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ ({Φ}^{-1}Φ)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ i.e., by substituting any column $c(t)$ of $Φ$ into the homogeneous system, we get\n\n$$\n{c}^{′}(t)=Ac(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}^{′}(t)$ is the corresponding column of derivatives in $Φ.$ As a result, this means that ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that $Φ\\text{ is a fundamental}$ matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370898 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c20cd9a-5734-5129-93db-55f6dc985b3a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing the Formulas for Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4177bf02-3210-53ab-96cf-fb76f60dd10f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a fundamental" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370900} {:answer/id #uuid "eb106d23-0829-587e-ad40-fa362b7c5765" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a square" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370901} {:answer/id #uuid "6d2e7fea-08a8-5ccf-bf62-4d8c1435e15c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is an invertible" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370902} {:answer/id #uuid "d83fbd79-dc6d-5a20-a7e9-a00d01a8c4f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is the identity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4177bf02-3210-53ab-96cf-fb76f60dd10f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a fundamental" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370900} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cfd8bfb-325d-5aca-bf38-9c2f5cfd8baf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370899} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b403cb04-b404-5958-a375-23ccacba6ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370905} {:answer/id #uuid "bc93939f-784f-5bd2-a06e-01c901f09508" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370906} {:answer/id #uuid "ea27b5ff-35f3-507c-befa-0b46ed6e3459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370907} {:answer/id #uuid "dd0153cc-0b11-5eb7-bdbe-f3047ef11b77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea27b5ff-35f3-507c-befa-0b46ed6e3459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370907} :answer-field/id #uuid "a12b31a8-f67e-5498-a5be-7efb12d5fc48" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370904} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ec0ac13-c7cf-540e-8215-7f0870d4ca29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370910} {:answer/id #uuid "9e3ac1ea-251b-5099-9cdb-3a635c1a3e68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370911} {:answer/id #uuid "6ffc6023-b283-5032-a492-f5fbf75b0ccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370912} {:answer/id #uuid "250a8faa-6c85-59f6-a384-7a76cf0040a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ec0ac13-c7cf-540e-8215-7f0870d4ca29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370910} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc12adc1-7b82-552e-8249-73aad151c210" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370909} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd2e044b-4138-5c34-96c2-e25c6753638b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370915} {:answer/id #uuid "05c46f52-5573-587f-9a5a-72a3afe10515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370916} {:answer/id #uuid "775251c8-f8da-55e1-a5ba-bd1095f7b547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370917} {:answer/id #uuid "dfd1ea36-266d-5e9d-ab64-dd49a2b83f60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05c46f52-5573-587f-9a5a-72a3afe10515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370916} :answer-field/id #uuid "204b409a-e944-5726-8dca-243415133732" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "018e497f-687a-502a-9607-05584c937b92" :question/math-academy-id "q-336713" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that {{field-1}} matrix.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines {{field-2}} by substitution.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting {{field-4}} into $\\text{L1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ i.e., by substituting any column $c(t)$ of $Φ$ into the homogeneous system, we get\n\n$$\n{c}^{′}(t)=Ac(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}^{′}(t)$ is the corresponding column of derivatives in $Φ.$ As a result, this means that ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that $Φ\\text{ is a fundamental}$ matrix.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$, $\\text{L4},$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Let's substitute ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$ from $\\text{L4}$ into $\\text{L3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+\\cancel{AΦu(t)}=\\cancel{AΦu(t)}+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L3}\\text{ and }\\text{L4}$ by substitution.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L7},$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Substituting\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φu(t) \\\\  & =Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370919 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c20cd9a-5734-5129-93db-55f6dc985b3a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing the Formulas for Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7111386a-e5d8-5cdb-a66f-f02dbd4ed587" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "line $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370921} {:answer/id #uuid "2a897221-37ea-5bb6-b275-4cfc67233526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370922} {:answer/id #uuid "fe3d5050-a532-515f-9518-7c2d0b76e796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "solution of the system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370923} {:answer/id #uuid "097d14c4-e611-5792-894f-b03f44e8142c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first shifting theorem" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a897221-37ea-5bb6-b275-4cfc67233526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370922} :answer-field/id #uuid "786bc030-8484-5517-bec4-36f305101b6f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370920} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8af13c11-5624-5e0c-9118-2d6f9ca35f22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370926} {:answer/id #uuid "48057f17-6d88-5f22-bcf4-10a4f70a368a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370927} {:answer/id #uuid "2947f62d-137b-56eb-8de6-fe5d245591e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370928} {:answer/id #uuid "740510ae-faed-57ce-8f5b-5aed3e69ec03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "740510ae-faed-57ce-8f5b-5aed3e69ec03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370929} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6cf70a8-1cbd-53e2-9bd4-426935bf38ec" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370925} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd565cff-a49c-5e9d-ab0c-9d34cb6f0755" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370931} {:answer/id #uuid "b8eae938-6216-58cb-9f21-b806fb0bc01f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370932} {:answer/id #uuid "0d874607-20bd-525b-80c1-90366ba06ff9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370933} {:answer/id #uuid "0c8480d0-e335-501a-b552-f2dffee3d1f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd565cff-a49c-5e9d-ab0c-9d34cb6f0755" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370931} :answer-field/id #uuid "8be118a1-9919-59ea-8c1e-65fad67ddc08" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370930} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db79a2da-5750-5445-8f21-aa3628e8d1d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370936} {:answer/id #uuid "d4551103-3910-5890-9bcb-bd3f7b1fb242" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370937} {:answer/id #uuid "daa51417-4bf4-59ee-876f-0f7cb5e5a9dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370938} {:answer/id #uuid "278c098f-e3e0-50d0-a2a2-f97098781652" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db79a2da-5750-5445-8f21-aa3628e8d1d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370936} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e9687ee-ae93-5b74-8503-3d6f73601d22" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7bec1847-0e18-5b85-901e-94baeab036e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-336715" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into the {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-2}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L7}$ into {{field-4}} ." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L2},$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Let's substitute ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$ from $\\text{L1}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ into the initial system of ODEs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =Ax(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t) & =AΦu(t)+f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into $\\text{initial system of ODEs}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are linearly independent. So, $Φ$ is invertible. Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{pre-multiplying by }{Φ}^{-1}$ both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\cdot Φ{u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ ({Φ}^{-1}Φ)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L7},$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Substituting\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φu(t) \\\\  & =Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L7}$ into  $\\text{L1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370940 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c20cd9a-5734-5129-93db-55f6dc985b3a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing the Formulas for Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c859135-a504-575a-9ade-d02e57c9eacb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370942} {:answer/id #uuid "39003678-daaf-54cb-b2f7-40134546e0f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17